WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.189
A 3D-printed rover

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:02.826
that picks up

00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:03.192
litter

00:00:03.726 --> 00:00:04.869
Meet MOSS an

00:00:04.681 --> 00:00:05.577
open-source

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:07.900
mostly 3D-printed rover

00:00:07.712 --> 00:00:08.843
built by metrox

00:00:08.655 --> 00:00:09.752
to collect litter

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.107
It rolls on

00:00:10.919 --> 00:00:12.534
tracks grabs trash

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.265
with a robotic

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:13.678
arm

00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:14.821
and drops it

00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:15.423
into a rear

00:00:15.235 --> 00:00:15.718
bin

00:00:15.857 --> 00:00:17.036
The idea started

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:17.743
while picking up

00:00:17.555 --> 00:00:18.863
trash in Thailand

00:00:19.406 --> 00:00:20.113
It went from

00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:21.068
concept to working

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.047
prototype in just

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:22.566
two months

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:23.545
with help from

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.040
Codex

00:00:24.088 --> 00:00:24.936
and the build

00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:25.797
is being shared

00:00:25.621 --> 00:00:26.941
openly so others

00:00:26.753 --> 00:00:27.672
can make one

00:00:28.206 --> 00:00:29.220
Full story on

00:00:29.031 --> 00:00:29.927
the dashboard
